{
  "title": "CMOS inverter VTC",
  "group": "Electronics — digital",
  "description": "CMOS inverter VTC: switching threshold vs PMOS width (Wp = 10/20/40 µm, balanced at 20 µm)",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 60,
        "y": -158,
        "title": "CMOS inverter VTC — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A CMOS inverter: VIN (dcsweep 0 -> 3.3 V) drives the",
          "shared gate of PMOS MP and NMOS MN; output is vout at",
          "the MP/MN drain. The sweep walks input through the",
          "switching region where both devices conduct.",
          "MP.W is stepped 10/20/40 um: widening the PMOS raises",
          "its drive, pushing the trip point Vm higher; the 20 um",
          "case balances MN and centers Vm near VDD/2.",
          "",
          "Set MP.W = 4e-05 and re-run to see Vm shift high."
        ]
      }
    ],
